Body:
> I have the same requirement. my case is that a large model needs to understand an image based on a URL.
> 
> The prompt is as follows: https://xxxxx/xxx.png please describe this image.
> 
> Opencode interprets the request to the large model as a text:
> 
> "messages": [
>     {
>       "role": "user",
>       "content": [
>         {
>           "type": "text",
>           "text": "https://xxxxx/xxx.png please describe this image",
>         }
>       ]
> but the format required for large models is as follows:
> 
>     "messages": [
>         {
>             "role": "user",
>             "content":
>             [
>                 {
>                     "type": "image_url",
>                    "image_url": "https://xxxxx/xxx.png"
>                 },
>                 {
>                     "type": "text",
>                     "text": "please describe this image"
>                 }
>             ]
>         }
>     ]
> I need a hook that can modify messages before making a request to the large model.

https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/blob/dev/packages/opencode/src/session/prompt.ts#L594

I looked at the code of OpenCode and found that it now supports modifying messages. Here is a demo:
```ts
export const MessagePlugin: Plugin = async (
  input: PluginInput,
): Promise<Hooks> => {
  const client = input.client;

  return {
    'experimental.chat.messages.transform': async (hookInput, output) => {
      for (const message of output.messages) {
        if (message.info.role !== 'user')
          return;

        const newParts: Part[] = [];

        await client.app.log({
          body: {
            service: 'message-plugin',
            level: 'info',
            message: 'user message',
            extra: {
              message,
            },
          },
        });

        for (const part of message.parts) {
          if (part.type === 'text') {
            // ...
            newParts.push(part);
        }

        if (newParts.length !== message.parts.length) {
          message.parts = newParts;
        }
      }
    },
  };
};

```

